{artist: Big & Rich }
{composer: Alpin; Rich }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h_OyFoxp_uo  (Capo 0)

TIP:  The intro is a bit cumbersome.  It starts with an (A6+) which is (A) with the 1st string/3rd fret covered.  Then slide the pinky down one fret for the (A6) and lift off for (A).  Alernatively you can play the (A6+) as a barre of the bottom 4 strings with your pinky covering 1st string/3rd fret, then lift off the pinky to play the (A6) and then lift off a little further so the 1st string is open for the (A).  You could also play the sequence as (Dsus4)(D) and then either (A) or (Dsus2).

TIP:  If you usually play the (F) as a barre or with your pinky covering the 5th string bass <c> you want to come off that 5th string and leave it open for the word “Five” in “Nineteen Sixty-Five.”  
  

